{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The housing mix proposed in the development would not respond to the identified housing need in the Borough as 76% of the units would be either studios or one-bed flats, contrary to Policy SC3 of the Hounslow Local Plan and H10 of the London Plan. ",
    "Reason : 2 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that affordable housing could not be included in the development or that it is maximised on the site, contrary to Policy SC2 of the Hounslow Local Plan.",
    "Reason : 3 - The development would comprise two tall buildings in Hounslow Town Centre but is of simple, bland design and form that lacks any visual interest or elegance and does not relate well to the character of the area, with a scale stretching immediately upwards on the fa�ade to 11 storeys, broken only with repetitive balconies at every level. The development is therefore contrary to Policies CC1, CC2 and CC3 of the Hounslow Local Plan and D4 of the London Plan. ",
    "Reason : 4 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the development would not result in unacceptable impacts on the daylight, sunlight and outlook of neighbouring residents, contrary to Policies CC2 and SC4 of the Hounslow Local Plan and Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan. ",
    "Reason : 5 - The standard of accommodation provided for future residents of the redeveloped site is considered unacceptable by virtue of poor light and outlook, both internally and on the balconies provided, and through a lack of private or communal outdoor space, contrary to Policies SC4 and SC5 of the Hounslow Local Plan, and Policy D6 of the London Plan. ",
    "Reason : 6 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate the impact of the scheme on highway capacity or road safety as no details have been provided of existing or anticipated vehicle movements during construction and use of the site, delivery/servicing details or other vehicle movements, no disabled parking has been provided, and cycle parking and accessibility is considered inadequate, contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2.  ",
    "Reason : 7 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the scheme would not result in unacceptable impacts on habitats and species, or that sufficient greening of the site would be provided, contrary to Local Plan Policy GB7. ",
    "Reason : 8 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the scheme would not detrimentally affect any buried archaeological features, given its location within an Area of Archaeological Interest relating to the London to Silchester Road, contrary to Policy CC4 of the Local Plan. ",
    "Reason : 9 - Insufficient information has been provided to determine whether the impact of the development on air quality, or on future residents due to poor air quality, would be acceptable, contrary to Local Plan Policy EQ4. ",
    "Reason : 10 - Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the development would not result in increased flood risk, and that surface water would be managed appropriate and sustainably, contrary to Local Plan Policy EQ3. "
  ],
